Settling the thread whose turn it is, or which pays for it, leaves its core unmarked.
A bind, an unbind or a lender handed the turn back gives the turn a request due later, or leaves it on spare time,
and nothing compares it with a thread due sooner on the run queue before the tick.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a thread waits with a deadline before the turn's request
Witness: fuzz bind-turn-later

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -496,7 +496,6 @@ static void thread_settle(struct thread *t)
     }
     /* What the turn runs on, and the request it runs, may have changed, so its core looks at its run queue again. */
     if (is_turn(t)) {
-        cores[t->core].run_stale = true;
         core_notify(&cores[t->core]);
     }
 }
